      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="verdict.reference.help" resname="verdict.reference.help">
        <source>The reference row: how the URL answered before the migration.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="verdict.referenceNotOk.help" resname="verdict.referenceNotOk.help">
        <source>The URL already fails on the reference, so there is nothing to compare. It is listed in the sitemap search engines know, though. Possible causes: a detail page (news, job offer, product) listed in the page sitemap that only works with a record in its URL; an error in a plugin or content element; a page for logged-in users only.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="verdict.ok.help" resname="verdict.ok.help">
        <source>Same path, same page or record.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="verdict.movedWithRedirect.help" resname="verdict.movedWithRedirect.help">
        <source>The URL redirects to the same page or record. Nothing to do, unless a warning says otherwise.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="verdict.missing.help" resname="verdict.missing.help">
        <source>The URL answers with an error on the target and does not redirect. Possible causes: the page was moved or renamed without a redirect; it was not migrated, is hidden or not translated; its slug changed; an error on the target itself — check the status code.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="verdict.redirectBroken.help" resname="verdict.redirectBroken.help">
        <source>The URL redirects, but ends in an error, a loop or too many redirects. Possible causes: the redirect target was deleted or moved; redirect rules lead into each other; rules for https, www or a trailing slash undo each other.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="verdict.otherContent.help" resname="verdict.otherContent.help">
        <source>The URL answers with 200, but shows a different page, record or language. Possible causes: a redirect to a parent or start page; the slug is used by another page now; a language fallback shows the default language.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="verdict.identityUnknown.help" resname="verdict.identityUnknown.help">
        <source>The URL answers with 200, but the markers needed for a comparison are missing. Possible causes: one environment does not render the page uid in the body tag or the record meta tag; a page template replaces the body tag.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="verdict.listed.help" resname="verdict.listed.help">
        <source>A page from the target sitemap, requested to suggest redirect targets.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="status.serverError" resname="status.serverError">
        <source>HTTP %1$s: server error</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="status.serverError.help" resname="status.serverError.help">
        <source>Possible causes: a detail page listed in the page sitemap that needs a record in its URL — the plugin fails without one; an exception in a plugin or content element; a database or configuration error on this environment. The TYPO3 log of this environment names the exception.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="status.notFound" resname="status.notFound">
        <source>HTTP %1$s: not found</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="status.notFound.help" resname="status.notFound.help">
        <source>Possible causes: the page was moved or renamed without a redirect; it is hidden, deleted or not translated; the record of a detail page no longer exists.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="status.accessDenied" resname="status.accessDenied">
        <source>HTTP %1$s: access denied</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="status.accessDenied.help" resname="status.accessDenied.help">
        <source>Possible causes: the page is restricted to logged-in users; Basic Auth for this environment is missing or wrong; a web server rule blocks the request.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="status.clientError" resname="status.clientError">
        <source>HTTP %1$s: request refused</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="status.clientError.help" resname="status.clientError.help">
        <source>The server refused the request. Possible causes: a web server or firewall rule, rate limiting, or arguments in the URL the site does not accept.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="status.noAnswer" resname="status.noAnswer">
        <source>No answer</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="status.noAnswer.help" resname="status.noAnswer.help">
        <source>The request got no HTTP answer. Possible causes: the host is unreachable, a DNS or certificate error, or a timeout — a higher --timeout may help.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="warning.redirectChain" resname="warning.redirectChain">
        <source>Redirect chain</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="warning.redirectChain.description" resname="warning.redirectChain.description">
        <source>More than one redirect before the final page. Point the first redirect directly at the final URL.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="warning.temporaryRedirect" resname="warning.temporaryRedirect">
        <source>Temporary redirect</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="warning.temporaryRedirect.description" resname="warning.temporaryRedirect.description">
        <source>The chain contains a 302, 303 or 307. A permanent move should answer 301 or 308.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="warning.redirectToRootPage" resname="warning.redirectToRootPage">
        <source>Redirect to start page</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="warning.redirectToRootPage.description" resname="warning.redirectToRootPage.description">
        <source>A deep URL redirects to a start page. Search engines often treat this as a soft 404.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="warning.listedUrlRedirects" resname="warning.listedUrlRedirects">
        <source>Sitemap URL redirects</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="warning.listedUrlRedirects.description" resname="warning.listedUrlRedirects.description">
        <source>The sitemap lists a URL that redirects. A sitemap should only contain final URLs.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="warning.languageChanged" resname="warning.languageChanged">
        <source>Language changed</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="warning.languageChanged.description" resname="warning.languageChanged.description">
        <source>The target page is in a different language than the reference page.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="warning.recordIdentityUnknown" resname="warning.recordIdentityUnknown">
        <source>Record unknown</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="warning.recordIdentityUnknown.description" resname="warning.recordIdentityUnknown.description">
        <source>Several URLs render this page without a record marker — probably a detail page. Which record is shown cannot be compared.</source>
